    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d483">

                <pb facs="0759" n="623" sameAs="frus:frus1929v01/pg623"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.79611 Tri-Motors Safety Airways/101:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Vice Consul at Port-of-Spain, Trinidad</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Demorest</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>[<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port-of-Spain</hi>,] <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Trinidad</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-08-20T16:00:00-04:00">August 20, 1929—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 6:04 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>The French Consul has volunteered the information to me that the French
                    Government has offered the British Government airways concessions <pb
                        facs="0760" n="624" xml:id="pg624"/> in French Indo China or French Africa
                    in exchange of similar concessions in British West Indies to Compagnie Generale
                    Aéropostale. The French Consul has informed Governor of Trinidad of connection
                    French company with Tri-Motors Safety Airways, Incorporated, (New York, Rio, and
                    Buenos Aires Line).</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Demorest</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
